From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] A headless wake's paused-turn lookup skips
 non-conforming profile dirs and serves no profile

Review t_01a1ceb9846fd38e (REQUEST_CHANGES at b59783b8): the successor lookup in
_wake_session_turn resolved every profiles/ entry through server._profile_home, which
raises ProfileUnavailableError for a name that is no valid profile id. One such directory
(with a state.db) made every headless wake of an unloaded chat return "error"; the parent
returned "started". _profile_home also registers each profile as served by this process
and activates multi-profile hosting, a side effect a read of turn markers must not have.

update_pause.paused_turn_homes resolves the homes read-only with
hermes_cli.profiles.get_profile_dir (the resolver _profile_home itself uses) and skips
names it refuses (ValueError).

RED on b59783b8: test_a_non_conforming_profile_dir_does_not_fail_the_wake
(assert 'error' == 'started') and test_a_fresh_pause_in_a_profile_home_is_left_to_its_successor
(assert 'error' == 'busy'). GREEN: the PR's 4 test files, 67 passed.
